      "writtenOn": "2018-03-08T00:12:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are 2 options as far as this is concerned.\n1. Let UiccCard/UiccProfile be null until we actually have a card present. This is the current intent, and if we go with this, we should have a different way to broadcast initial ABSENT when card is absent on bootup.\n2. Always have a non-null UiccCard/UiccProfile corresponding to a phone. This would be similar to earlier implementation that we had with IccCardProxy.\n\nWhat you have implemented is midway. UiccCard/Profile are not null after the first IccCardStatus is received, and they are also null on radio state absent. This creates these windows of null values which I feel is not ok. We should go with one of the 2 options, and I am in favor of #1 unless you see issues with that. Let me know what you think.",
